// REJECTS: Field 'persister' should be specified only once
//
// The `persistence` rule is `BRACE_OPEN (documentation | trigger | service |
// serviceOutputTargets | persister | notifier | tests)* BRACE_CLOSE` -- one flat unordered
// star over the entire element. Nothing in it says "at most one persister", and nothing says
// "at most one doc" either; every such rule is a validateAndExtract* call in
// visitPersistence.
//
// Two persisters is the version of that worth pinning because the two here disagree: one
// Streaming and one Batch, i.e. the element would have to be both kinds at once.
###Persistence
Persistence test::persistence::neg::TwoPersisters
{
  doc: 'an element with two persisters';
  trigger: Manual;
  service: test::persistence::Service;
  persister: Streaming
  {
    sink: Relational
    {
      database: test::persistence::Database;
    }
  }
  persister: Batch
  {
    sink: Relational
    {
      database: test::persistence::Database;
    }
    ingestMode: NontemporalSnapshot
    {
      auditing: None;
    }
    targetShape: Flat
    {
      modelClass: test::persistence::ModelClass;
      targetName: 'TestDataset1';
    }
  }
}
